<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Certificate pinning — STATUS: HONEST-DISABLED (structure documented,
    pins NOT active).

    The <pin-set> blocks are COMMENTED OUT below. Android's <pin-set> is
    strict: any live pin element that does not match the cert chain fails
    the connection, so shipping a placeholder pin would brick every
    request. Uncomment ONLY after capturing real SPKI hashes.

    To ACTIVATE pinning:
      1) `node scripts/capture-spki.mjs <host>` for each domain — prints
         current-leaf + current-issuer SPKI SHA-256 in base64.
      2) Uncomment the <domain-config> block, replace the ...=== SPKI-SHA256
         markers with the captured hashes (leaf FIRST as primary, issuer
         SECOND as backup — a rotated leaf keeps working while the issuer
         stays the same).
      3) Set `expiration="YYYY-MM-DD"` to the earliest cert expiry so a
         stale build fails OPEN (unpinned) rather than bricking installed
         users when both pins expire.
      4) Ship an app update. A pin rotation without an app update WILL
         break installed users — Android accepts that trade. Keep a backup
         pin one issuer ahead.

    Every request through CapacitorHttp (capacitor.config.json) routes
    through the native stack and would honour this file once activated.
    Vault seed / wallet-core signing never touch these hosts.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <domain-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true">
        <domain includeSubdomains="true">localhost</domain>
        <domain includeSubdomains="true">10.0.2.2</domain>
    </domain-config>

